+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+Requests the authenticated user's conversation list. Available only when `transport.history.enabled` is `true`. The user id is taken from the connection, never from the frame.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_conversations",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": {
+    "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
+    "sessionId": "s1"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                             |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                                  |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | How many summaries to return; integer 1–200             |
+| `before` | object | No       | Cursor to resume a page; `{updatedAt: string, sessionId: string}` — both fields required |
+
+`before` is a composite cursor rather than a bare timestamp, so paging never drops a conversation when two share an activity time.
+
+- `list_conversations` is accepted by `validateMessage` as a known type; `limit: 0`, `limit: 201`, a non-integer `limit`, a non-number `limit`, and a non-object `before` are each rejected with an error that names the offending field ([validated by: accepts list_conversations as valid and rejects it with any bad limit or non-object before, naming the field](../../src/transport/ws/conversation-list.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
+- With `transport.history.enabled: true` and a store whose `listFor` returns three summaries, the server answers exactly one `conversation_list` frame with three summaries whose `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are ISO strings, and no `stream_end` ([validated by: with history enabled and three conversations in the store, answers list_conversations with one conversation_list carrying three summaries with ISO string dates and no stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/conversation-list.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- The user id is taken from the session, not the frame: a frame carrying an extra `userId` field is answered with the connecting user's own list, and `limit` and `before` are forwarded to `listFor` as sent ([validated by: calls listFor with session.userId regardless of a userId field in the frame, forwarding limit and before](../../src/transport/ws/conversation-list.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+- When `transport.history` is absent, the server answers `UNSUPPORTED`; a store that implements no `listFor` is answered the same way, so a misconfiguration reads as a service limitation, not as a database failure ([validated by: with history absent answers UNSUPPORTED and no conversation_list; with history on but no listFor on the store, also UNSUPPORTED](../../src/transport/ws/conversation-list.acceptance.test.ts#L137)).
+- A `list_conversations` frame is answered off the per-session lock and arrives before the `stream_end` of a `user_message` that is still streaming ([validated by: answers list_conversations while a user_message is streaming, before that stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/conversation-list.acceptance.test.ts#L159)).
+
